{"at":"2026-10-19T20:46:55.160Z","event":"prompt","agent":"remakecraft:observer","by":"main","sha256":"d04634a63fa0f4dd1a87a281c57e316fd02bcbd90943dbaa49002113d4d5f896","prompt":"Build the complete inventory for the remake run of \"guessling\", a command-line character-encoding detector.\n\n- App tree: guessling (remake.json there: stack web, mode clean)\n- Room: guessling.remake-room\n- Plugin root: <plugin>\n- Evidence: <room>/evidence/ — two documentation pages, 218 encoded text samples, labels.json (expected encoding per sample) and INDEX.md. Read INDEX.md first.\n- Original, black box only (clean mode: never open, read, decompile or grep anything in <room>/original/; only execute it):\n  node guessling.remake-room/original/detect.mjs [--minimal] [-l] [-e ERA] [file ...]\n  It reads stdin when no file is given. Run it on the evidence samples and on crafted inputs to observe output format, every flag, multi-file output, stdin naming, empty input, binary/undetectable input, nonexistent files, bad flags, exit codes, stderr vs stdout, and how --minimal, -l and -e ERA change results. Compare its output to labels.json and record where they agree and differ.\n- Blocked terms (existing reimplementations, off-limits): chardet, uchardet, charset-normalizer, cchardet, chardetng, jschardet. Do not search for or consult them.\n\nWrite inventory.json (and anything else your role writes) inside the room only. Every observable behaviour gets a stable id. Note that the conformance tests will check the encoding name only, never the confidence number, so record the encoding set and naming precisely. End with a short summary: counts by category, and the UNKNOWN list (behaviour you could not pin down and what evidence would resolve it)."}
