{"at":"2026-10-20T06:50:45.189Z","event":"prompt","agent":"remakecraft:builder","by":"main","sha256":"ac81632264ecb860c8dc68211d3fa83ea74291b3ed9292e385c13eeb691de874","prompt":"Build features `cli.era-option`, `cli.era-value-parsing` and `cli.era-syntax` of the guessling clone (a Node CLI character-encoding detector), and lay down the era-aware detection framework the remaining detection features need. This also fixes review must-fix M2: the stopgap detector src/detect/koi8r.mjs ignores the chosen era and reports KOI8-R in eras where the spec wants None or another name.\n\n- App tree: guessling (your own worktree, from current main). Read remake.json, spec/spec.json + spec/spec.md (v2), tests/visible/. Run the visible suite with `node scripts/run-suite.mjs tests/visible --bin bin/guessling.mjs` and save the passing list BEFORE changing anything.\n- Plugin root: <plugin>.\n- Current state: src/args.mjs parses -e/--encoding-era (a missing value is recorded as null); src/cli.mjs has checkEra (rejects invalid values through argError, exit 2). The era value is never upper-cased or defaulted, so detectors get \"dos\" or undefined instead of MODERN_WEB. src/detect/index.mjs returns one result per detector with no era tagging, there is no 200,000-byte cut, and there is no step after selection for the -l rename.\n- Do this:\n  1. Normalise the era (case-insensitive, default MODERN_WEB, last value wins, the syntax forms the spec gives) and pass it to detection.\n  2. Restructure src/detect/index.mjs so each detector/encoding declares which eras it belongs to (from the spec's per-era name lists), detection only considers encodings allowed in the chosen era (plus the always-on set the spec names), and a single post-selection hook exists where cli.legacy will apply the -l rename later. Leave a clear place to apply the input-limit cut. Document the detector contract in a short comment at the top of index.mjs.\n  3. Make the KOI8-R stopgap era-correct under that framework, or remove it if the spec's era tables make it wrong everywhere it currently answers. Don't regress the tests that pass today unless they passed only through the era bug; name any such test.\n- In parallel another builder is implementing --help/--version in src/cli.mjs. Keep your cli.mjs edits to the era path.\n- Scratch files go in a `.scratch/` folder inside your worktree (git-ignored), never in `.remake/`.\n- Done: every cli.era-option, cli.era-value-parsing and cli.era-syntax visible test that does not need detection not yet built passes, and nothing regresses (diff the lists). Commit on your branch. Report before/after counts, the detector contract, and any blocked tests."}
