{"at":"2026-10-20T07:15:10.460Z","event":"prompt","agent":"remakecraft:builder","by":"main","sha256":"d6c05a6c3bfbef0f3ff7fb9bbeb7d0cdc124dc888957266d4febabf1fa9b6c52","prompt":"Guessling clone (a Node CLI character-encoding detector), phase 5 batch 2. Your work: the staged detection pipeline (review must-fix), plus features `detect.unicode-no-bom`, and the spec v2 updates to `detect.empty-binary` and `detect.ascii`.\n\n- App tree: guessling (your own worktree from current main; the v2 tests were just published). Read remake.json, spec/spec.json + spec/spec.md (v2), tests/visible/, and .remake/reports/review.md (the latest review). Run the visible suite with `node scripts/run-suite.mjs tests/visible --bin bin/guessling.mjs`. Save the passing list to `.scratch/` BEFORE changing anything; use the Write tool if shell redirects are refused.\n- Plugin root: <plugin>.\n- Must-fix from review: in src/detect/index.mjs a detector can only add candidates and the highest confidence wins, so no stage can end detection with a final answer or a final \"no result\". Restructure it into ordered stages, each of which can return a final result, a final \"no result\", or pass:\n  1. BOM\n  2. binary/NUL/control rejection (spec v2: NUL inside short text gives None in every era, random and NUL-heavy bytes give None, including in ALL)\n  3. BOM-less UTF-16/32 (detect.unicode-no-bom, including the Japanese BOM-less UTF-16 → None rule)\n  4. escape encodings (a slot only: another builder does detect.escape later)\n  5. ascii\n  6. multibyte and single-byte scoring\n  Keep the era filtering and the postSelect hook. Each scorer must return every candidate above its floor, not just its best. Make the 200,000-byte window configurable for a future library entry. Update the contract comment.\n- Don't key results on specific test inputs; use rules the spec states (byte ratios, not length cut-offs).\n- In parallel: another builder works on cli.legacy (the postSelect rename in index.mjs) and the CLI side. A third adds a UTF-8 detector module (detect.utf8, utf8-invalid, ascii-esc, input-limit) that will register as a stage-6 scorer. Coordinate through the contract: leave a clear registration point.\n- Scratch files go in `.scratch/` (git-ignored), never in `.remake/`.\n- Done: the staged pipeline is in, the detect.unicode-no-bom, detect.empty-binary and detect.ascii visible tests pass apart from ones that need detectors not built yet (list them), and nothing that passed before fails (diff the lists). Commit on your branch. Report before/after counts and the new contract."}
{"at":"2026-10-20T07:15:11.305Z","agent":"remakecraft:builder","id":"aa514c056e3d5a3f4"}
{"at":"2026-10-20T07:15:20.029Z","event":"prompt","agent":"remakecraft:builder","by":"main","sha256":"a47a369dd2a35792363d56e1ed5d040f43f918ef2feb989a9342286e42b6f881","prompt":"Guessling clone (a Node CLI character-encoding detector), phase 5 batch 2. Your features: `cli.legacy`, `cli.legacy-casing`, `cli.stdin-tty-notice`, `cli.parsing-conveniences`, the spec v2 change to `cli.stdin` (stdin named twice after a large stdin repeats the result), and review finding S6 on src/help.mjs.\n\n- App tree: guessling (your own worktree from current main; the v2 tests were just published). Read remake.json, spec/spec.json + spec/spec.md (v2), tests/visible/, and .remake/reports/review.md. Run the visible suite with `node scripts/run-suite.mjs tests/visible --bin bin/guessling.mjs`. Save the passing list to `.scratch/` BEFORE changing anything; use the Write tool if shell redirects are refused.\n- Plugin root: <plugin>.\n- Implement:\n  - The -l rename map from spec v2, including ISO-8859-6→Windows-1256 and ISO-8859-8→Windows-1255. Apply it in the postSelect hook in src/detect/index.mjs; keep that edit minimal, because another builder is restructuring index.mjs at the same time. If cleaner, put the map in its own module, e.g. src/legacy.mjs, called from postSelect.\n  - The casing rule: renamed names use the `Windows-` spelling, directly detected ones keep `WINDOWS-`.\n  - The stdin tty notice: wording per spec, on stderr, only for a character device.\n  - The `- -` repeat after a large stdin, per spec. Don't invent a precise threshold the spec doesn't give; pick a reasoned one and say which.\n  - Any parsing conveniences still missing.\n  - S6: the help text must be the clone's own words, not a copied stock phrase, and must describe -l correctly: it renames, it does not widen the era.\n- Many cli.legacy tests need detectors that aren't built yet (Windows, ISO, EUC-KR pages). Implement the rename logic and unit-check it against the spec's map; list the tests that are blocked on detection.\n- Scratch files go in `.scratch/` (git-ignored), never in `.remake/`.\n- Done: all non-blocked tests of these features pass, and nothing that passed before fails (diff the lists). Commit on your branch. Report before/after counts and the blocked tests."}
{"at":"2026-10-20T07:15:20.866Z","agent":"remakecraft:builder","id":"a9f5c10c69e107e6f"}
{"at":"2026-10-20T07:15:28.027Z","event":"prompt","agent":"remakecraft:builder","by":"main","sha256":"9b444be4f223368a8b16b79fbe61b822eb58b9993e24b3bba391e22337225af9","prompt":"Guessling clone (a Node CLI character-encoding detector), phase 5 batch 2. Your features: `detect.utf8`, `detect.utf8-invalid`, `detect.ascii-esc` and `detect.input-limit`.\n\n- App tree: guessling (your own worktree from current main; the v2 tests were just published). Read remake.json, spec/spec.json + spec/spec.md (v2), tests/visible/, and .remake/reports/review.md. Run the visible suite with `node scripts/run-suite.mjs tests/visible --bin bin/guessling.mjs`. Save the passing list to `.scratch/` BEFORE changing anything; use the Write tool if shell redirects are refused.\n- Plugin root: <plugin>.\n- Current main: src/detect/index.mjs has the era framework. The contract is at the top of the file, and inputWindow() is where the 200,000-byte cut is applied. In parallel, another builder is restructuring index.mjs into ordered stages (BOM → binary rejection → BOM-less UTF-16/32 → escape → ascii → scorers). Your code should be a self-contained module, e.g. src/detect/utf8.mjs, registered as a scorer through the existing contract with a minimal registration edit. Keep it easy to move into the scorer stage.\n- Behaviour from spec v2: UTF-8 validity and when UTF-8 is reported per era, including:\n  - a short line with one multibyte character gives utf-8;\n  - one multibyte character inside long ASCII text gives a single-byte page, not utf-8, so your confidence must reflect the share of multibyte content;\n  - a truncated E2 82 at the end gives utf-8 in MODERN_WEB and ALL;\n  - stray ESC in otherwise ASCII text gives utf-8;\n  - the window rules.\n  The spec's quirks are observed behaviour: implement them as rules, never key on specific test inputs.\n- Tests that need single-byte pages (the WINDOWS-1252/1250 outcomes) are blocked until the single-byte scorer exists. Make your confidence low enough in those cases that a single-byte scorer can win later, and list the blocked tests.\n- Scratch files go in `.scratch/` (git-ignored), never in `.remake/`.\n- Done: all non-blocked tests of these features pass, and nothing that passed before fails (diff the lists). Commit on your branch. Report before/after counts, your confidence model in two lines, and the blocked tests."}
