{"at":"2026-10-20T07:26:30.427Z","event":"prompt","agent":"remakecraft:builder","by":"main","sha256":"635aa054e675c8835831110134355947094d5b29a7d633b0c52ae5efc9bf3379","prompt":"Guessling clone (a Node CLI character-encoding detector), phase 5 batch 3. Your feature: `detect.escape`, the escape-based encodings (ISO-2022-JP, ISO-2022-KR, HZ-GB-2312 and anything else the spec lists), available in every era per spec.\n\n- App tree: guessling (your own worktree from current main). Read remake.json, spec/spec.json + spec/spec.md (v2), and tests/visible/. Run the visible suite with `node scripts/run-suite.mjs tests/visible --bin bin/guessling.mjs` and save the passing list to `.scratch/` BEFORE changing anything; use the suite's report-file argument and the Write tool if shell redirects are refused.\n- Plugin root: <plugin>.\n- Pipeline: src/detect/index.mjs runs ordered stages, and stage 4 is the escape stage. Push `{ run }` into `ESCAPE_DETECTORS`; run returns PASS, done(result, eras?) or NO_RESULT (see src/detect/stage.mjs). The ascii stage passes on ESC and on `~{`, and src/detect/utf8.mjs reports utf-8 for stray ESC in otherwise 7-bit text. Your stage must claim only real escape-encoded text, and PASS otherwise so stray ESC still reaches utf-8.\n- Spec v2 rules:\n  - ISO-2022-JP designators.\n  - The ISO-2022-KR header alone is enough.\n  - HZ needs `~{ … ~}` with valid GB2312 byte pairs between the markers. Bare `~{ ~}` around English is NOT HZ: it must PASS so it ends up utf-8.\n  - Check how -l and the era interact with these per spec.\n  Don't key on specific test inputs.\n- Stay in your own module (e.g. src/detect/escape.mjs) plus a minimal registration edit in index.mjs. Another two builders are adding scorers in parallel. Scratch files go in `.scratch/` (git-ignored), never in `.remake/`.\n- Done: the detect.escape visible tests pass, and nothing that passed before fails (diff the lists). Commit on your branch. Report before/after counts and any blocked tests."