{"at":"2026-10-20T07:35:45.857Z","event":"prompt","agent":"remakecraft:builder","by":"main","sha256":"67e588c8fdf803d321bbe03de2135622e82d766b61f6e721d42f962f1b5585b3","prompt":"Guessling clone (a Node CLI character-encoding detector): fix two reviewer must-fixes. Details are in .remake/reports/review.md, items M1 and M2.\n\n- App tree: guessling (your own worktree from current main). Read spec/spec.json + spec/spec.md (v2) and tests/visible/.\n- Save the passing list before you change anything: run `node scripts/run-suite.mjs tests/visible --bin bin/guessling.mjs` and save the result to `.scratch/` (git-ignored; never put scratch in `.remake/`). Use the suite's report-file argument and the Write tool if redirects are refused.\n\n**M1 (stage order):** the binary stage in src/detect/index.mjs and binary.mjs runs before the escape and ascii stages. It refuses ASCII text that contains occasional control bytes, such as BEL inside text and nroff overstrike (char BS char). Spec detect.ascii says those are ascii.\n- Reorder so the pipeline runs: BOM, the empty/NUL-heavy check, wide (UTF-16/32), escape, ascii, then the control-byte ratio check, then scoring.\n- Once the order is right, remove the ISO-2022-KR SO/SI special case in binary.mjs, if the escape stage now runs first and makes it unnecessary.\n- Keep every currently passing test passing.\n\n**M2 (wide false positive):** src/detect/wide.mjs reports pure-ASCII text like `1,0,1,0,0,0,1,0,1,0\\n` or `a b c d e f g h\\n` as utf-16le at high confidence. The UTF-16 shape rule must require actual zero bytes in the high-byte column, per spec (\"many zero bytes\"). Plain 7-bit text with no NULs must never be UTF-16/32.\n\nAnother builder is adding a single-byte scoring engine in parallel (new modules plus a registration line in index.mjs), so keep your index.mjs edit confined to the stage order. Done: both fixed, with a quick check that the reviewer's example inputs now give ascii (write the probe files with the Write tool into `.scratch/`); visible suite has no regressions (diff the lists); committed on your branch. Report before/after counts."}
