{"at":"2026-10-20T08:21:29.149Z","event":"prompt","agent":"remakecraft:reviewer","by":"main","sha256":"741124498f96807d6c00c2478a05b073d58b5b084732867b2a6f6d158c873ee1","prompt":"Final review of the guessling clone (a Node CLI encoding detector) against spec v2. All 40 features are built, the visible suite passes 173/173, and the remaining budget is small, so keep this review focused and economical: about 25 tool calls at most.\n\n- App tree: guessling\n- Plugin root: <plugin>\n- Your previous report is .remake/reports/review.md. Review the range c613220..HEAD.\n\nWhat's in that range:\n- the Mac, ISO, regional, DOS and EBCDIC tiers in src/detect/sbcs/: charts-*.mjs, affinity.mjs, utf8-fallback.mjs, relocate.mjs, and the engine and pages changes;\n- commit b73250c, which addresses your M3 (own UTF-8 curve), M5 (home-page tie-break), S6 (HZ Hanzi check) and S9 (punctuation-only Western text).\n\nCheck, in priority order:\n1. Are M3, M4, M5 and M6 resolved? Is anything still copied from the original or a blocked reimplementation (formulas, tables, constants)?\n2. Is there input-keyed or fixture-tuned logic?\n3. Are there clear spec violations?\n4. Note that three overlapping mechanisms (affinity, utf8-fallback, relocate) do similar jobs. Flag this only if they produce wrong results.\n\nScratch probes go in .remake/tmp/ (the wall allows only that). Classify findings as must-fix, should-fix or nit, update your report, and report the counts and the must-fix list."}
