{"at":"2026-10-20T08:27:08.905Z","event":"prompt","agent":"remakecraft:builder","by":"main","sha256":"9f941a58f7140144405fa31727e4a10fdc3de122002185647b5e616f9857a903","prompt":"Guessling clone (a Node CLI character-encoding detector): fix four reviewer must-fixes in src/detect/sbcs/. Each one breaks a spec v2 rule (spec/spec.json + spec/spec.md).\n\n**Bash rules:** one plain command per call; no `cd`, no `&&`/`;` chains, no redirects. Write probe scripts with the Write tool into `.scratch/` (git-ignored, never `.remake/`) and run them with `node .scratch/x.mjs`. Commit with `git add -A` then `git commit -m \"...\"` as separate calls, on your worktree branch.\n\nBefore you change anything, run `node scripts/run-suite.mjs tests/visible --bin bin/guessling.mjs` and note the result (currently 173/173). It must stay there.\n\n- **M7:** ISO-8859-8 has no table, so it drops out of PAGES and can never be reported (pages.mjs ~:229 and the ERA_PAGES lists).\n  - Add the page. TextDecoder has `iso-8859-8`.\n  - Spec rows (detect.era-always-on): Bulgarian MacCyrillic text gives ISO-8859-8 in LEGACY_ISO, DOS and MAINFRAME.\n  - Implement it generically if that falls out of reasonable modelling (a Hebrew page reading Cyrillic Mac bytes as its best fit in eras without Cyrillic pages). Don't key on the file.\n  - At minimum, Hebrew ISO-8859-8 text must be detected where the spec lists the page.\n- **M8:** fresh German MacRoman text is read as Turkish CP857 at 0.80. The spec wants WINDOWS-1252 in MODERN_WEB, MacRoman in LEGACY_MAC, CP850 in DOS and MacRoman in ALL. Today it gives 1250, MacTurkish, CP857 and CP857 (pages.mjs ~:161, affinity.mjs ~:100-111).\n  - Find out why German reads as Turkish through CP857: probably the shared umlaut slots plus Turkish's ğ/ş/ı readings.\n  - Fix the language scoring so German wins, without overfitting.\n- **M9:** Bulgarian and Russian CP855 text is never a candidate. DOS gives CP866 and ALL gives CP1125 (pages.mjs ~:159). Check the CP855 chart against the published IBM CP855 layout; it's probably wrong, or its language viability excludes bg/ru.\n- **M10:** the fallback paths (utf8Fallback, relocate, affinity in index.mjs ~:82-86) are added after settleTies runs, so they skip the home-page tie rule. Fresh French UTF-8 in LEGACY_ISO gives ISO-8859-16 where the spec says ISO-8859-1. Route the fallback candidates through the same tie settlement, and carry `near`/`uncapped` or the language ids so the home-page rule applies.\n\nFor each fix, write a fresh sample in your own words in the right language and encoding with the Write tool and Buffer/TextEncoder (Node can encode only latin1/utf8 natively, so build byte arrays from the chart where needed). Show before and after.\n\nAlso, if cheap: S14. Icelandic is defined twice in languages.mjs (in the identify-only block and the DOS block) with different statistics. Unify them into one definition.\n\nDone: the four fixes are probed, the visible suite is still 173/173, and the work is committed. Report briefly."}
